content.text:
Now app.js main. This is the biggest. Need implement carefully.

Let's outline code.

Imports:
```
import { WIDTH,HEIGHT, SKIN_TONES, HAIR_COLORS, EYE_COLORS, HAIR_STYLES, BACKDROPS, PALETTES, TOOL_CATEGORIES, TOOLS, CHALLENGES, DEFAULT_MODEL, shade, rgba, mix } from './data.js';
import { geometry, renderBase, drawBackdrop, drawHairBack, drawSkinBase, drawFeatures, drawHairFront, drawOverlay } from './face.js';
import { SoundKit } from './audio.js';
```

Constants:
```
const LAYER_IDS = ['bg','hairBack','skin','underMakeup','blush','highlight','eyeshadow','features','eyeMakeup','lipstick','hairFront','overlay'];
const PAINT_LAYERS = ['underMakeup','blush','highlight','eyeshadow','eyeMakeup','lipstick'];
const STORAGE_KEY='glam-studio-v1';
```
DOM refs helper `$ = id => document.getElementById(id)`.

State:
```
const persisted = load();
const state = {
 mode:'free', challengeId:null,
 model:{...DEFAULT_MODEL},
 tool:'lipstick', category:'lips', color: PALETTES.lipstick[2].color,
 size:1, strength:1, soundOn: persisted.soundOn !== false,
 progress: persisted.progress||{}, coins: persisted.coins||0,
 history: [], future: [], drawing:false, pressed:null,
 activePointers: new Map()
}
```

Layer creation:
```
const layers = {};
const scene = $('faceScene');
const interaction = document.createElement('canvas'); interaction.width=WIDTH...
for id of LAYER_IDS: create canvas, class `layer-${id}`, aria-hidden, append.
interaction.className='interaction'; append.
contexts...
```
But confetti is separate canvas in HTML inside faceShell, not faceScene. Good.

Interaction z-index 20, confetti z30.

`setupCanvas(canvas)` sets width/height.
`getCtx(id)`.

Static:
```
function renderStatic() {
  renderBase(layers, state.model);
}
```
`renderBase` expects layers object of DOM canvases; works.

High DPI not needed. For hero, create offscreen layer canvases.

Hero:
```
function renderHero() {
 const hero = $('heroCanvas'); const ctx=hero.getContext('2d');
 const temp={};
 LAYER_IDS.forEach(id=>{ temp[id]=document.createElement('canvas'); temp[id].width=WIDTH...});
 renderBase(temp,{...DEFAULT_MODEL, style:'waves', backdrop:'rose'});
 // apply demo makeup on temp.underMakeup etc
 const tctx = ...
 // under makeup: subtle contour/highlight? use helper paintSoftEllipse etc.
 // eyeshadow gold/rose gradient clipped geometry.shadow.
 // lipstick red.
 // blush.
 // eyeliner.
 // highlight.
 // Overlay already.
 // composite all layers
 ctx.clearRect...
 LAYER_IDS.forEach(id=>ctx.drawImage(temp[id],0,0))
 // frame? maybe no.
}
```
Need draw makeup onto offscreen clipped. Implement helper `fillClipped(layer, clipPath, painter)`.

Maybe demo makeup: rose-gold eyes, deep red lips, dewy blush, gold highlight. Use direct gradients:
```
const ec=temp.eyeshadow.getContext('2d'); ec.save(); ec.clip(geometry.shadow);
let g=ec.createRadialGradient(343,470,4,343,470,100); stops #b96b3f .55 -> transparent; fill rect
gold shimmer: radial at (330,460)... 
```
Lip: `lipstickCtx.save(); clip(lips); fill linear gradient #b3123a to #6e0e2a; restore;` Then add slight gradient. Blush: radial. Highlighter: radial white. Liner: stroke upper path (need geometry.leftUpper/rightUpper paths) with lineWidth 6 dark. Then composite.
- Also maybe draw freckles? not for hero.
- Need update overlay gloss which is there. Fine.

Interaction and clipping:
```
const CLIP_PATHS = {face: geometry.face, lips: geometry.lips, eye: geometry.eye, shadow: geometry.shadow, cheeks: geometry.cheeks, highlight: geometry.highlight}
```

prepare stroke:
```
function beginStroke(e) {
  if (state.busy) return;
  const point = getPoint(e);
  if (!point) return;
  state.drawing = true;
  state.lastPoint = point;
  state.affected = [];
  state.strokeStartHistory();
  const tool = TOOLS[state.tool];
  const targets = tool.layer ? [tool.layer] : PAINT_LAYERS;
  for id of targets {
    const ctx = contexts[id]; const clip = CLIP_PATHS[tool.clip] || CLIP_PATHS.face;
    ctx.save();
    if (tool.clip) {ctx.beginPath();...} // Path2D clip: ctx.clip(clip)
    ctx.globalCompositeOperation = tool.id==='eraser'? 'destination-out':'source-over';
    ctx.lineCap='round'; ctx.globalAlpha=1;
    prepared.push({id,ctx});
    // For layers other than tool.layer if eraser, clip each to its own clip? For eraser, we want clear makeup anywhere; each layer already has its own clipped content, but if we clip eraser to face for underMakeup etc. Use layer-specific clips:
  }
  ...
  drawAt(point, first=true);
}
```
For tool.layer, clip tool.clip. For eraser, for each layer, use per-layer clip from `LAYER_CLIP` map:
```
underMakeup:'face', blush:'cheeks', highlight:'highlight', eyeshadow:'shadow', eyeMakeup:'eye', lipstick:'lips'
```
For paint, target layer one and clip tool.clip (same as layer's clip). Fine.

But if we clip at begin and keep state until end, strokes drawn outside clip are ignored. For eraser, non-target layers? We apply erase to all layers with each clip.

Snapshot before drawing:
```
function snapshot() {
 const entry = PAINT_LAYERS.map(id=>({id,data:layers[id].toDataURL('image/png')}));
 state.history.push(entry); if>18 shift
 state.future=[]
 updateHistoryButtons()
}
```
But capturing all six every stroke is heavy; PNG toDataURL each maybe 10-50ms. Could capture only affected layers and store `{id,data}`; undo requires restore only those layers. For eraser all layers. For paint one layer. Good.
- `capture(layerIds)` returns array of {id,data}.
- History entry is array. Undo: for each item, store current data into redo entry {id,current}, then restore. Need asynchronous image load. Manage:
```
let restoring=false;
async function restoreEntry(entry) {
 state.busy=true;
 await Promise.all(entry.map(item => new Promise(resolve=>{ const img=new Image(); img.onload=()=>{ctx.clearRect...; ctx.drawImage(img,0,0); resolve()}; img.onerror=resolve; img.src=item.data;})));
 state.busy=false; updateMeters();
}
async function undo() {
 if(restoring||!history.length) return;
 const entry=history.pop();
 const inverse=[];
 for(item of entry){ inverse.push({id:item.id,data:layers[item.id].toDataURL('image/png')}); }
 state.future.push(inverse);
 await restoreEntry(entry);
 ...
}
```
Note dataURL of empty layer is still fine.
- On undo we need each item's layer. Good.
- For clear all, push snapshot of non-empty layers? Simpler snapshot all 6. Then clear all. This allows undo. Great.
- For randomize, snapshot all then apply.
- When model/challenge changes, clear makeup without history? Could push history; but challenge selection should reset. Do `clearMakeup({record:false})`.

`updateHistoryButtons`.

Drawing:
```
function drawDab(ctx, tool, p, last) {
 const radius = (tool.brush * state.size) / 2? Wait tool.brush is diameter maybe. Use radius = tool.brush * state.size * 0.5? For lip 24 -> radius 12, quite small. Maybe brush is radius. 24 px radius on 900 canvas. On screen 600 wide => 16 px, okay. Eyeshadow 36 radius => 24 px screen. Good. Use radius = tool.brush*state.size. Readout show diameter? Show round(brush*size) px. fine.
 interp distance = max(2, radius*0.22); steps...
 for each point stamp.
}
```
For freckles stamps, spacing bigger and dots random.

`stamp(ctx, x,y,r,color,alpha,softness)`:
```
const g=ctx.createRadialGradient(x,y,0,x,y,r);
g.addColorStop(0, rgba(color, alpha));
g.addColorStop(Math.min(0.75, 0.15+softness*0.45), rgba(color, alpha*0.85));
g.addColorStop(1, rgba(color,0));
ctx.fillStyle=g; circle fill
```
For hard liner use softness low: stops: 0 alpha; 0.72 alpha; 1 0. The tool alpha already.
For freckles special:
```
const count = 4+random*5;
for ... dot at x+rand*radius*0.9 etc, radius 0.9+1.8, alpha .5
```
Need not accumulate too much.

Alpha handling: context globalCompositeOperation; set on prepare. For highlighter maybe use 'lighter' but keep source-over. For gloss maybe 'screen'. Actually if gloss draws white source-over on lipstick, it's visible. Fine.

`drawAt(p)`:
- `const tool=TOOLS[state.tool]`
- if freckles: special stamps in target ctx.
- else interpolation from last to p.
- For each target ctx (eraser multiple) draw stamps.
- update state.lastPoint.

Coordinate mapping.

On pointerdown: ensure audio unlocked (sounds). Hide hint. prevent default. set pointer capture. `beginStroke`. On pointermove with buttons or state.drawing, draw. On pointerup finish.
- Could support multi-touch? Only primary. Ignore if not drawing.
- On pointercancel finish.
- Also pointer leaves with capture still.

`finishStroke` restores each prepared ctx, updates meters debounce, sfx swipe, triggers particles? no.

Model render and clip: clipping path static independent of model, good.

Color selection:
```
function selectTool(toolId, opts) {
 state.tool = toolId; state.category=TOOLS[toolId].category;
 if (!opts.keepColor) {
   const pal = PALETTES[TOOLS[toolId].palette];
   // if current color exists in palette, keep it, else pick default index? 
   const exists = pal.find(c=>c.color===state.color);
   state.color = exists? state.color : pal.find(p=>p.color===default?)...
 }
 renderTools, renderSwatches, update hints
